    893:| §P.P4 batched-x k-tuple narrow-window count, slot 1 — empirical baseline. Build sieve-shared batched-x evaluator pi_H(x_i; w) = #{n in [x_i, x_i+w] : n+h prime for all h in H}; measure per-x amortised cost vs M for k in {2 (twin H=(0,2)), 3 (admissible H=(0,2,6)), 4 (admissible H=(0,2,6,8))} at x in {10^6, 10^7}; check whether the Thread-5 / S224 Correlation Dichotomy 33x speedup transposes to k-tuple counts. | EMPIRICAL (B-PARTIAL-POSITIVE: dichotomy direction transposes, magnitude smaller — 5x at 10^6 / 8x at 10^7 vs Thread-5's 33x — k-independent within +/-10% across k=2,3,4) | E (E1.5 + S224 + S418..S421 — first cross-x-axis experiment for narrow-window k-tuple counts in the project; positive direction) | Thread 9 commit step 1/(>=3) (S429). Built `experiments/analytic/k_tuple_batched/slot1_baseline.py`: naive_ktuples (per-x segmented sieve) + batched_ktuples (single sieve over [min(x), max(x)+w+h_max], walk M offsets) + singular_series (HL constant) + hl_estimate_window (linear-w HL approximation) + verify_small (sympy cross-check) + harness over (x_max in {10^6, 10^7}) x (k in {2, 3, 4}) x (distribution in {uncorrelated Uniform[x_max/2, x_max], corr_w=M consecutive integers, corr_w=polylog [x_anchor, x_anchor+log^2 x]}) x (M in {1, 4, 16, 64}). 72/72 cells counts_match=1. **Headline ratio T_batched/T_naive at M=64**: corr_w=M / corr_w=polylog rows are 0.188-0.213 at 10^6 (5x speedup) and 0.119-0.135 at 10^7 (8x speedup), k-independent within +/-10% across k=2,3,4. Uncorrelated rows are 9-49x (worse than naive — anti-amortising shared-sieve over Theta(x_max/2) range; structural finding, not bug; same as Thread 5's uncorrelated finding after fixing algorithm-side reduction to naive). **Why magnitude smaller than Thread 5's 33x**: per-query naive cost is O(sqrt(x) * log log x * w) segmented-sieve, NOT O(x^{2/3}) Lucy DP — amortisation ceiling is lower since baseline is already polylog-in-w. Speedup grows with x as predicted-and-confirmed sqrt(x) * log l