LRH = Hardy-Littlewood Random-Residual Hypothesis**: three asymptotic statements on cross-h ensembles at fixed x — (a) first-moment vanishing (1/N)Σr_∞(x,h_i) = o(√li_2), (b) second-moment asymptotic to F²_H·S̄_H·li_2(x), (c) cross-h decoherence E_x[r_∞(h_i)·r_∞(h_j)] = o(S̄_H·li_2). HLRH is the cross-h analogue of S195 random-phase + S244 Montgomery pair-correlation transposed K-axis → h-axis; implied by strong k-tuple HL conjecture (k=4) plus GUE-side correlations on prime-pair-count joint distributions; currently unproven beyond Bombieri-Davenport linear-bound levels. **Corollary B' (C-B')**: for h-batches with max h ≤ (log x)^β and |H| ≤ poly(log x), the full HL_∞ evaluator costs O(N·√(max h)) ⊆ poly(log x) per batch with cross-h L²-typical error ε_typ(x, H) ≤ (1+o(1))·F_H·√(S̄_H·li_2(x)) ≍ F_H·√(S̄_H·x)/log x. **Knee Corollary**: under truncation profile ⟨ε_Q²⟩_H ≍ C(H)/Q² (slot-3 ensemble: C(H) ≈ S̄²_H·h_max/Q_max), Q* = √(C(H)·li_2(x)/(F²_H·S̄_H)) ≍ √x/log x. Empirical validation: 10⁷ predicted 196, knee 199-200; 10⁸ predicted 543, knee 599-1009. **Direct K↔h analogy (slot 4 §8)**: bilinear form Σ_{j,k>K}y^{ρ_j+ρ̄_k}/(ρ_j ρ̄_k) ↔ (1/N)Σ_{i,j∈[N]}r_∞(x,h_i)r_∞(x,h_j); diagonal "j=k → 1/|ρ_j|² sum" ↔ "i=j → r²_∞ average"; off-diagonal close-pair (Montgomery suppression) ↔ HLRH(c) cross-h decoherence; far-pair (RH-only Riemann-von Mangoldt) ↔ k-tuple HL for k=4. **Two structural weakenings** vs Thread 7: (i) F_H ensemble-dependent in [0.36, 0.70] vs Thread 7's universal F_GUE = 0.755 ± 0.06 across decades; (ii) HLRH (k-tuple HL + prime-pair-count joint distribution correlations) is less-studied than RH + Montgomery (the canonical analytic-NT conditional setting). **What this rules out**: (i) a Cramér-model F_H = 1 prediction for cross-h variance — empirically rejected at 0.36-0.70 across slot 2/3 cells; (ii) the hypothesis that cross-h decoherence is automatic from unbiasedness alone (HLRH(a) suffices without HLRH(c)) — the proof requires both for Q ≪ Q*. **What