    872	| §P.P1 batched-on-modulus q amortisation, slot 1 — per-(q, a) explicit-formula evaluator with three-axis decoupled cost (zero-database setup ⊥ per-χ partial-sum eval ⊥ orthogonal χ̄(a) sum): does the zero database admit cross-character sharing for χ of the same conductor q, and is per-character evaluation cost x-independent? | REFINEMENT (architecture + empirical baseline) | I (slot-1 baseline; slot 2-5 attack the χ-amortisation question) | Thread 6 commit step 1/5 (S227). Built `experiments/analytic/batched_q_amortisation/per_q_a_explicit_formula_profile.py` — three-axis decoupled evaluator: `time_zero_db_setup(q, K)` (per-character cache build), `time_per_chi_eval(zeros, x)` (vectorised numpy partial sum Σ_ρ x^ρ/ρ for one χ at one x), `time_orthogonality(q)` (χ̄(a) · ψ_χ vector dot of length φ(q)). Profiled at q ∈ {101, 1009, 10007} for x ∈ {1e6, 1e8} and K ∈ {50, 200, 800}. Synthetic non-principal-χ zeros via Riemann-von Mangoldt density inversion (numpy-vectorised Newton); principal-χ zeros from cached ζ-zeros. **Q1 — T_zero_db_setup shape**: linear in φ(q)·K with constant ~2.7µs per (χ, K-zero), held to within 5% across three decades of q. **No naive cross-character zero sharing** at the database level — zeros for distinct χ of the same conductor are structurally independent (block-GUE statistics with O(1/T) cross-character correlation, asymptotically negligible at K = 800 / x = 10⁶). **Q2 — T_per_chi_eval x-dependence**: x-independent within measurement noise (10⁶ vs 10⁸ identical to µs); ~50ns per zero asymptotically (numpy K=800 vectorised). Same scaling as Thread 5 ζ-zero primitive. **Q3 — Orthogonality vs evaluation**: orthogonality is 2-4 orders of magnitude subdominant for q ≤ 10⁴ (3.8 µs at q=101, 336 µs at q=10007 vs full_per_x of 1.9 ms / 268 ms respectively). Per-(q, a) cost is dominated by φ(q)·T_per_chi_eval. **a-direction batching amortisation**: at q=1009, K=200, x=10⁶, varying a with M ∈ {1, 4, 16, 64, 256}: T_amort/a goes 188 → 64 → 33